WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER

HyperBlade and HYPERX.EXE are the property of their respective rights holders.

The source here is a reconstruction of HYPERX.EXE. To compile to the same bytes it has to
reproduce the original's string literals, constants and data tables, and its few
hand-written assembly routines. Those are in the source.

No original binary or game data is in this repository, and neither is a disassembly
listing or a Ghidra database. docs/logo.png and docs/gameplay_soft.png show the game's
art, for identification only. You supply your own copy of HyperBlade, and every
build reads what it needs from that copy.

Addresses, sizes, function names and the measurements under progress/ and symbols/ are
facts about the program, recorded so the reconstruction can be checked. They are not the
program.

Nothing in this licence grants any right to HyperBlade itself. You need your own copy,
and what you may do with it is between you and its rights holders.


